---
props {
  variant: "sale" | "new" | "low-stock" | "default" = "default"
}
---

{*
  A block tag cannot appear inside an attribute expression: {match} in a
  class={...} is a hard parse error. The conditional class-list form is the
  way to map a prop onto a class. Each entry is "name": condition, and an
  entry whose condition is falsy is left out.
*}
<span class={
  "badge",
  "badge--sale": variant == "sale",
  "badge--new": variant == "new",
  "badge--low-stock": variant == "low-stock",
  "badge--default": variant != "sale" && variant != "new" && variant != "low-stock"
}>
  <slot />
</span>

<style>
.badge {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
  border-radius: 9999px;
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.badge--sale      { background: #fef2f2; color: #b91c1c; }
.badge--new       { background: #f0fdf4; color: #15803d; }
.badge--low-stock { background: #fffbeb; color: #b45309; }
.badge--default   { background: #f3f4f6; color: #374151; }
</style>
